<title>UK: SOCCER-MCDONALD LEAVES QPR AFTER 17 YEARS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-MCDONALD LEAVES QPR AFTER 17 YEARS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Former Northern Ireland captain Alan McDonald signed a two-year contract with Swindon on Tuesday, ending a 17-year career at Queens Park Rangers.</p>
<p>McDonald, 33, who won 53 caps for Northern Ireland and captained his country for six seasons, joined Swindon on a free transfer.</p>
